hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24263","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Yazid ibn Abi Habib al-Misri narrated to me, from Irak ibn Malik al-Ghifari, I heard Nawfal ibn Mu'awiyah al-Dili, while he was sitting with Ibn Umar in the market of Madinah, say: A prayer, whoever misses it, it is as though his family and wealth have been taken away, his family and wealth taken. He said: So Abdullah, meaning Ibn Umar, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is al-Asr."
"24264","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, and Hashim, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nawfal ibn Mu'awiyah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever misses the prayer, it is as though his family and wealth have been taken away. Hashim said in his hadith: So I said to Abu Bakr: What is this? He said: Al-Asr. And Yazid said in his hadith: So I said: What is this prayer? He said: I do not know. Al-Zuhri said: As for this hadith which Abu Bakr narrated to us, Salim narrated it to us, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever misses the Asr prayer, it is as though his family and wealth have been taken away."
"24265","Fazarah ibn Umar narrated to us, Ibrahim, meaning Ibn Sa'd, narrated to us, Ibn Shihab narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Muti' ibn al-Aswad, from Nawfal ibn Mu'awiyah al-Dili, like the hadith of Abu Hurayrah regarding tribulations, except that Abu Bakr adds: Among the prayers is a prayer, whoever misses it, it is as though his family and wealth have been taken away."
